module

public import Mathlib.Topology.Compactness.Compact

import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Quasi-compact spaces

Stacks 005A (1) calls a topological space `X` *quasi-compact* if every open covering of `X`
has a finite subcover. Mathlib's notion is `CompactSpace X`, which says that `Set.univ` is
compact in the filter sense (no Hausdorff condition is imposed). This file proves the two
agree: `CompactSpace X` holds if and only if every family of open sets covering `X` has a
finite subfamily covering `X`.

Items (2) and (3) of Stacks 005A are Mathlib's `IsSpectralMap` (a continuous map under which
the preimage of every compact open is compact) and `IsRetrocompact`, both registered there.

## Main results

* `compactSpace_iff_finite_subcover`: `CompactSpace X` iff every open covering of `X` has a
  finite subcover.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 005A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/005A)
-/

@[expose] public section

open Set

add_to_stacks 005A "(1): a quasi-compact topological space is `CompactSpace`; see
  `compactSpace_iff_finite_subcover` for the open-cover characterization" CompactSpace

/-- **Quasi-compact spaces.** A topological space is compact (Mathlib's `CompactSpace`, with no
separation axiom) if and only if every open covering of it has a finite subcover: for every
family `𝒰` of open subsets with `⋃₀ 𝒰 = univ` there is a finite `𝒱 ⊆ 𝒰` with `⋃₀ 𝒱 = univ`.

The forward direction is `IsCompact.elim_finite_subcover_image` for `univ`; the converse is
`isCompact_generateFrom`, the topology being generated by its open sets. -/
@[stacks 005A "(1): a space is quasi-compact if every open covering has a finite subcover"]
theorem compactSpace_iff_finite_subcover {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] :
    CompactSpace X ↔ ∀ 𝒰 : Set (Set X), (∀ U ∈ 𝒰, IsOpen U) → ⋃₀ 𝒰 = univ →
      ∃ 𝒱 ⊆ 𝒰, 𝒱.Finite ∧ ⋃₀ 𝒱 = univ := by
  rw [← isCompact_univ_iff]
  constructor
  · intro h 𝒰 h𝒰 hcov
    obtain ⟨𝒱, h𝒱, hfin, hsub⟩ :=
      h.elim_finite_subcover_image (b := 𝒰) (c := id) h𝒰 (by simp [← sUnion_eq_biUnion, hcov])
    exact ⟨𝒱, h𝒱, hfin, univ_subset_iff.1 (by simpa [← sUnion_eq_biUnion] using hsub)⟩
  · intro h
    refine isCompact_generateFrom (TopologicalSpace.generateFrom_setOfPred_isOpen _).symm
      fun P hP hs => ?_
    obtain ⟨Q, hQ, hfin, hQs⟩ := h P hP (univ_subset_iff.1 hs)
    exact ⟨Q, hQ, hfin, hQs.ge⟩
